guide forever/reputation/ravenholdt
title Ravenholdt Reputation
category Reputation
folder Reputation · World
levels 24-60
zone Alterac Mountains
keywords Ravenholdt, Ravenholdt Manor, Syndicate, Fahrad, Myrokos Silentform, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, Syndicate Emblem, Heavy Junkbox, Junkboxes Needed, pickpocket, rogue, Lord Tomas, Barton, Anastasia Miller, Stromgarde, Strahnbrad, Durnholde Keep
why The assassins' guild: Forever's new rogue quests, then Syndicate kills and Heavy Junkboxes to Exalted.
reward text Ravenholdt reputation (no vendor or reward in Forever's data)

# Built from Forever's data: the quest rows of the Ravenholdt quests with Forever's reputation values (The
# Manor, Ravenholdt 6681 and the Forever-new rogue quests 96779-96786, 100 to 300 each; Syndicate Emblems
# 6701, 100 per emblem; A Simple Request to The Azure Key 8233-8236; Junkboxes Needed 8249, 50 per five
# Heavy Junkboxes where Classic Era paid 75), the standing windows from the world database (Syndicate Emblems
# only below Friendly), the Syndicate spawns and their pickpocket rates for the Syndicate Emblem (9 to 27%),
# and Forever's client faction table (everyone starts Neutral 0). Neutral to Exalted is 42,000 reputation.
# The world database has no kill reputation for the Classic Syndicate mobs, and Forever's data holds no
# Ravenholdt vendor or reputation-gated item.
# The places of Barton's report, the Northfold footlocker, Anastasia Miller, her stash, the shipment box and
# the two Perenolde heirlooms are player reports from the Forever beta (the data has no spawn for them).
# ASSUMED: Syndicate humans give 5 Ravenholdt reputation per kill up to the end of Honored (11,999/12,000;
# Classic flow; Forever's data has no kill reputation rows for them). In-game check: does a Syndicate kill in
# Alterac raise Ravenholdt, and where does it stop?
# The rogue quests pay 700 in all (The Manor 100, Syndicate Sabotage 100, What's the Big Idea? 100, Covert
# Extraction 100, The Syndicate Sting 300; A Way In, Master of Disguise and Ain't No Telling pay nothing), so
# 23 emblems finish Friendly. Heavy Junkboxes bind to no one (client item table): rogues can trade and sell them.
# INGAME: grey-mob kill rep (Classic: about a fifth). Every Syndicate is level 41 or lower, grey at 60.
# INGAME: Covert Extraction (96782): Forever's in-game dialog captures have Myrokos offering it, but its page
# lists it for the Alliance: does Myrokos offer it to Horde rogues after What's the Big Idea?

step The Manor, Ravenholdt
  only Rogue
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip Rogues from level 24: ask your class trainer in a capital "May I have it, please?" for the Elegant Letter, and read it. The path up to the manor starts in the hills north of Durnholde Keep. In the tunnel on the way lies a chest: do not open it (an elite guard jumps out), just walk past it to earn the Rite of Cunning. Fahrad waits on the manor's balcony.
  accept 6681 item 17126              -- Elegant Letter, from your class trainer
  kill 13936 quest 6681.1             -- walk past the trapped chest in the tunnel
  zone Alterac Mountains
  turnin 6681                         -- Fahrad: 100 reputation

step Myrokos Silentform
  only Rogue
  tip Myrokos Silentform, in the manor, has Forever's new rogue quests: 100 reputation each for Syndicate Sabotage, What's the Big Idea? and Covert Extraction, which follows it, and 300 for The Syndicate Sting at the end of the Stromgarde chain (A Way In and the two quests after it pay nothing). All can be done solo with stealth from level 30; below that, the Master of Deception talent and a Flash Powder for Vanish help.
  accept 96779
  accept 96781
  accept 96783

step Durnholde Keep: Lord Tomas
  only Rogue
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip Lord Tomas is inside Durnholde Keep, the Syndicate fortress east of Southshore. Stealth past the guards in the courtyard.
  kill 266216 quest 96779.1           -- Lord Tomas

step Strahnbrad: Barton
  only Rogue
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Barton hides in a house in Strahnbrad, among stealthed Syndicate. Pick his pocket for the report; Distract turns him around if you are under his level.
  collect 275482 quest 96781.1 @62.6,46.9 -- Barton's Scouting Report: pickpocket Barton

step Northfold Manor: a uniform
  only Rogue
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip The Syndicate Footlocker stands among the Syndicate camps of Northfold Manor, north of Stromgarde. Open it to finish A Way In and take the Syndicate Uniform.
  turnin 96783 object 656157 @32.3,26.6 -- Syndicate Footlocker
  accept 96784 object 656157 @32.3,26.6

step Stromgarde: Anastasia Miller
  only Rogue
  tip Put on the Syndicate Uniform and go into Stromgarde. Anastasia Miller waits on a ledge just outside the castle; players reach her by jumping from the roof of the house beside the ledge. Her stash is upstairs in a house near the keep.
  turnin 96784 npc 266847 @26.8,64.4  -- Anastasia Miller
  accept 96785 npc 266847 @26.8,64.4
  collect 275709 quest 96785.1 @29.5,65.1 -- Stolen Funds, in Anastasia's Stash upstairs
  turnin 96785 npc 266847 @26.8,64.4
  accept 96786 npc 266847 @26.8,64.4

step Thoradin's Wall: the shipment
  only Rogue
  tip The hand-off is at the southern end of Thoradin's Wall, in the west of the Arathi Highlands: two Syndicate guard the box. Kill them or lure them off, then take the Intercepted Shipment. Keep the uniform: Myrokos wants it back.
  collect 275882 quest 96786.1 @15.5,43.0 -- Intercepted Shipment

step Back to Myrokos
  only Rogue
  zone Alterac Mountains
  turnin 96779                        -- 100
  turnin 96781                        -- 100
  turnin 96786                        -- 300
  accept 96782 npc 13085 optional     -- Covert Extraction, after What's the Big Idea?

step Ruins of Alterac: the Perenolde heirlooms
  only Rogue
  when onquest 96782
  tip The two heirlooms lie in two towers of the Ruins of Alterac, the ogre-held ruin in the middle of the Alterac Mountains. The tower with the sword is ringed by elite ogres: stay in stealth. Neither item is guarded once you are inside.
  collect 275636 quest 96782.2 @41.4,40.2 -- Royal Aegis of Perenolde, the shield
  collect 275635 quest 96782.1 @38.5,58.0 -- Blade of House Perenolde, the sword
  turnin 96782                        -- Myrokos Silentform: 100

step Syndicate Emblems to Friendly
  only Rogue
  tip Neutral to Friendly is 3,000 reputation; the quests above pay 700 of it. Any Ravenholdt Guard on the path takes Syndicate Emblems, 100 reputation each, until you reach Friendly: 23 emblems after the quests. Pick the pockets of Syndicate humans; they never drop emblems when killed. The Arathi camps pay best: Syndicate Prowlers and Conjurors carry one about a quarter of the time. Kill what you have robbed so the next ones respawn fresh.
  zone Arathi Highlands
  collect 17124 x5 optional @30.0,27.0 -- Syndicate Emblem: pickpocket Syndicate
  zone Alterac Mountains
  accept 6701 optional
  turnin 6701 optional                -- a Ravenholdt Guard: 100 per emblem
  rep 349 Friendly

step Syndicate kills to the end of Honored
  tip Everyone, not only rogues: in Classic every Syndicate human gave Ravenholdt 5 reputation up to the end of Honored (11,999 of 12,000) and not one point more, so 0 to there is 4,200 kills (3,600 after a rogue's quests and emblems). This step ticks at Honored; keep killing until the bar stops moving, then go on to the junkboxes. The highest Syndicate are in the north-west of the Alterac Mountains, Syndicate Assassins and Enforcers (level 38-40), with Syndicate Sentries (36-37) nearer the middle. At 60 all Syndicate are grey, and in Classic grey kills gave about a fifth: farm them before 48 if you can. Legacy Diplomat adds up to 10%.
  goto 38.3,15.4 "Syndicate Assassins and Enforcers"
  goto 47.4,17.5 "Syndicate Sentries"
  loop
  kill 2246 optional                  -- Syndicate Assassin, level 38-39
  kill 2247 optional                  -- Syndicate Enforcer, level 39-40
  kill 2243 optional                  -- Syndicate Sentry, level 36-37
  rep 349 Honored

step A Simple Request, rogues 50+
  only Rogue
  when level>=50
  tip At level 50 your class trainer has another letter for you, and Lord Jorach Ravenholdt a short chain: 360 reputation in all. The Sealed Azure Bag drops from Timbermaw Shamans in northern Azshara (about 1 in 27, or pick their pockets); the Encoded Fragments from Forest Oozes in Azshara (4 in 5). The Azure Key comes from Morphaz, an elite drake deep in the Temple of Atal'Hakkar: a five-player dungeon, group up.
  level 50
  zone Stormwind City
  accept 8233 npc 918 only Alliance   -- Osborne the Night Man, Stormwind
  zone Orgrimmar
  accept 8233 npc 3328 only Horde     -- Ormok, Orgrimmar
  zone Alterac Mountains
  turnin 8233                         -- Lord Jorach Ravenholdt
  accept 8234
  zone Azshara
  collect 19775 quest 8234.1          -- Sealed Azure Bag: Timbermaw Shamans
  turnin 8234                         -- Archmage Xylem
  accept 8235
  collect 20023 x10 quest 8235.1      -- Encoded Fragment: Forest Oozes
  turnin 8235
  accept 8236
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  collect 20022 quest 8236.1 optional @70.2,45.2 -- Azure Key: Morphaz, Temple of Atal'Hakkar (group)
  zone Alterac Mountains
  turnin 8236 optional                -- Lord Jorach Ravenholdt: 150

step Heavy Junkboxes to Exalted
  tip From the top of Honored to Exalted is 21,001 reputation, and Junkboxes Needed is the only way: Fahrad pays 50 and a Dusksteel Throwing Knife for every five Heavy Junkboxes (Classic Era paid 75), 421 turn-ins and 2,105 boxes. Boxes count at any standing, so take the cheap kills to their cap first. Any class can hand them in. Rogues get them by picking the pockets of humanoids around level 50 and up: Lower Blackrock Spire and Blackrock Depths are the classic spots, pick every pocket, reset and go again. The boxes do not bind, so everyone else buys them from rogues or at the auction house. Hand them in unopened; an opened box you empty vanishes, so leave one item in it.
  level 50
  zone Searing Gorge
  collect 16885 x5 optional @32.1,94.7 -- Heavy Junkbox: pickpocket level 50+ humanoids, Blackrock Mountain
  zone Alterac Mountains
  accept 8249 optional
  turnin 8249 optional                -- Fahrad: 50 per five boxes
  rep 349 Exalted
